From 93a54a522ac5d44356022c815927e7b80d30d123 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genetixteam <genetixteam@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:38:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: mt7915: give DBDC band1 its own MAC (from the EX20v v1
 port)

The EX20v describes the MT7915 DBDC chip with one OF node carrying one
mac-address from the romfile, so mt76_eeprom_override() gives phy0 and
phy1 the same address. Bump band1 to the next address when it collides
with band0. Taken from the v1 port (Emre Yavuzalp), refreshed for the
current mt76 revision.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YbeF2izcaoFj6qx1YBoB3j
---
 .../100-mt7915-dbdc-distinct-band1-mac.patch  | 33 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mt76/patches/100-mt7915-dbdc-distinct-band1-mac.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/100-mt7915-dbdc-distinct-band1-mac.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/100-mt7915-dbdc-distinct-band1-mac.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..225908f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/100-mt7915-dbdc-distinct-band1-mac.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: distinct band1 MAC on single-node DBDC
+
+Boards that describe the MT7915 DBDC chip with a single OF node carrying one
+"mac-address" (e.g. TP-Link EX20v, whose unique per-device MAC lives in the
+romfile, not the generic MediaTek radio EEPROM) make mt76_eeprom_override()
+apply that same device MAC to both bands, so phy0 (2.4 GHz) and phy1 (5 GHz)
+share one hardware address. Bump band1 to the next MAC when it collides with
+band0 after the override, keeping the vendor OUI (base+1 -> base+2). Boards
+that supply genuinely distinct per-band addresses are unaffected.
+
+Signed-off-by: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
+---
+diff --git a/mt7915/init.c b/mt7915/init.c
+index 51e6f495..03d4cb03 100644
+--- a/mt7915/init.c
++++ b/mt7915/init.c
+@@ -787,6 +787,15 @@ mt7915_register_ext_phy(struct mt7915_dev *dev, struct mt7915_phy *phy)
+ 	if (ret)
+ 		return ret;
+ 
++	/* Boards that describe the DBDC chip with a single OF node and one
++	 * "mac-address" (e.g. TP-Link EX20v) make mt76_eeprom_override() apply
++	 * the same device MAC to both bands. Bump band1 to the next address so
++	 * the two PHYs never share a hardware MAC, keeping the vendor OUI
++	 * (band0 = base+1 -> band1 = base+2).
++	 */
++	if (ether_addr_equal(mphy->macaddr, dev->mphy.macaddr))
++		eth_addr_inc(mphy->macaddr);
++
+ 	/* init wiphy according to mphy and phy */
+ 	mt7915_init_wiphy(phy);
+ 
